# Reference checksum for the CITE-seq arm (arm C).
#
# CITE_seq_lfc_plot.png is byte-identical to LNtest-overleaf/figures/
# CITE_seq_lfc_plot.png, verified 2026-09-10. That makes arm C the second arm
# whose committed output can be checked against the manuscript itself, after
# the clustering arm -- and unlike that one, nobody knew until the layout audit
# turned it up.
#
# It is ggsaved by citeseq/R/pbmc10k_metrics.R from CITE_seq_results.csv, which
# citeseq/exp.py writes. So the chain from memory_CD4.h5ad to a published figure
# is verifiable end to end, which is not true of any other arm.
#
# The companion CITE_seq_lfc_error_plot.png is NOT in the manuscript's figures/
# and is not hashed here; it sits in citeseq/results/ with the other outputs.
#
# To verify, from reproducibility/:
#     shasum -a 256 -c reference/citeseq/checksums.sha256
#
fa9bd50f30366c64d34ba66d6dbe3c64878625861963b98df279926bad75b3b3  reference/citeseq/CITE_seq_lfc_plot.png
